melody:
# Refrain as published in 1924 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; 3-beat pickup)
It had to be you,
D4 E4/ D4/ E4/ F#4/ ~F#4(4) ~F#4
it had to be you,
F#4 G4/ F#4/ G4/ G#4/ ~G#4(4) ~G#4
I wan-dered a-round and fin-al-ly found
G#4 A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4. G4/ A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4.
the some-bod-y who
G4/ A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4(4) ~B4
could make me be true,
A4 B4/ A4/ B4/ D5/ ~D5(4) ~D5
could make me be blue,
B4 A4/ B4/ A4/ G4/ ~G4(4) ~G4
and e-ven be glad just to be sad
G4 G4/ F#4/ G4/ A4/ ~A4(2) G4/ F#4/ G4/ A4/ ~A4(2)
think-ing of you.
B4/ E5/ B4/ A4/ ~A4(4) ~A4
Some oth-ers I've seen
D4 E4/ D4/ E4/ F#4/ ~F#4(4) ~F#4
might nev-er be mean,
F#4 G4/ F#4/ G4/ G#4/ ~G#4(4) ~G#4
might nev-er be cross or try to be boss,
G#4 A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4. G4/ A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4.
but they would-n't do,
G4/ A4/ G#4/ A4/ B4/ ~B4(4) ~B4
for no-bod-y else gave me a thrill,
B4 B4/ C5/ D5/ E5/ ~E5(2) E4/ F#4/ G4/ A4/ ~A4(2)
with all your faults I love you still.
A4/ B4/ C5/ D5/ ~D5(2) A4/ B4/ A4/ G4/ ~G4
It had to be you, won-der-ful you,
F#4 E4/ D4/ E4/ F#4/ ~F#4(2) E4/ D4/ E4/ F#4/ ~F#4(2)
had to be you.
B4/ D5/ B4/ G4/ ~G4(4) ~G4(2) r(2)
